It is an evergreen climber growing to {{convert|3|-|6|m|ft|0|abbr=on}}, with heart-shaped glossy leaves to {{convert|30|cm|0|abbr=on}} long, and occasionally spathes of white flowers in mature plants. With a minimum temperature requirement of {{convert|15|C|F|abbr=on}}, in temperate regions it must be grown under glass or as a houseplant. Under the synonym Philodendron scandens it has gained the Royal Horticultural Society's Award of Garden Merit. P. hederaceum have simple leaves that are arranged in an alternate fashion, meaning single leaves are born on alternating nodes.
